<title>USA: Equity Residential Properties Q4 FFO up.</title>
<headline>Equity Residential Properties Q4 FFO up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> FFO Shr		    $0.85		    $0.70</p>
<p> FFO			 56,077		   36,638</p>
<p> Revs		     134,300		  105,600</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  55,540		   44,424</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is Equity Residential Properties Trust.</p>
<p>Q4 1996 funds from operations (FFO) before $9,062,000 in preferred distributions vs $5,328,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Q4 1996 net income $43.4 million vs $30.4 million.  </p>
<p>Q4 1996 net income after $378,000 write-off of unamortized costs on refinanced debt.</p>
<p>			YEAR</p>
<p> FFO shr		    $3.12		    $2.75</p>
<p> FFO			189,282		  131,074</p>
<p> Revs		     478,400		  390,400</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  51,302		   43,983</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full-year 1996 FFO before $29,015,000 in preferred distributions vs $10,109,000.</p>
<p>Full-year 1996 net income $101.7 million vs $67.7 million.</p>
<p>Full-year 1996 net income after $3.5 million writeoff of unamortized costs on refinanced debt. Full-year 1995 results after $2.0 million gain on early extinguishment of debt.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
